PicoGKRuntime 26.2 (0f26321c) — VO4: a zero-length flat-capped lattice beam
renders nothing instead of NaN. Upstreamable to leap71/PicoGKRuntime; not yet
offered.

Applied to vendor/PicoGKRuntime by scripts/fetch-deps.sh after 0001-0007.
Kept as a patch because it modifies dependency source; no flag-level override
exists. Ledger row U30 (upstream/LEDGER.md).

Lattice::AddBeam already drops a zero-length beam with round caps (it is a
sphere, added as one). A zero-length beam with flat caps fell through:
LatticeBeam::fSdvFlatCone divides by the squared beam length, so every sample
in the beam's bounding box evaluated to NaN (729 of 729 in the audit probe),
and DoRenderLattice's min(NaN, existing) then overwrote existing geometry in
that box with active NaN voxels. A flat disc of zero thickness encloses
nothing, so the beam is now dropped. Output changes only for lattices that
contain such a beam, whose result was NaN-corrupted before.
--- a/Source/PicoGKLattice.h
+++ b/Source/PicoGKLattice.h
@@ -238,6 +238,15 @@
             return;
         }
         
+        if (!bRoundCap && ((vecS-vecE).fLength() < std::numeric_limits<float>::epsilon()))
+        {
+            // A flat-capped beam of zero length is a disc of zero thickness:
+            // it encloses nothing. fSdvFlatCone divides by the squared
+            // length, so rendering it would write NaN over every voxel in
+            // its bounding box, existing geometry included.
+            return;
+        }
+        
         m_oBeams.emplace_back(  vecS,
                                 vecE,
                                 fRadS,
